  "term": "embolism",
  "definition": "In this source, embolism refers specifically to pulmonary embolism, a serious form of venous thromboembolism that can occur after surgery. It is described as a potentially fatal postoperative complication, with risk linked here to cancer-related increased clotting and postoperative immobility.",
